                 make up Enumeration District 1, keyed by its own volunteers
                 from a scan of the same NARA microfilm T623 that IPUMS's
                 Ancestry-sourced extract (ipumsfullcount) draws on -
                 independent of IPUMS in both organization and scan. Read in
                 full, image by image, on 28 September 2026: 2,535 people,
                 1,553 White and 936 Black, with 46 whose race its indexers
                 could not read. Checked against the IPUMS extract's 2,490 for
                 the same enumeration district (residents_by_district_race,
                 race-by-district-1900-arlington): the two independent
                 transcriptions differ by only 45 people, and both are far
                 short of the roughly 2,989 Arlington district would need to
                 reach its published 3,200 once Fort Myer's 211 is added. The
                 shortfall recurring on two unrelated digitizations of the
                 schedules is the evidence that it is not a transcription gap
                 - the missing people are not on either surviving copy of the
                 schedule, so no further reading closes it},
